WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Name the canonical universe. A ranked row belongs to a declared symbol list—not an accidental search result or a remembered watchlist.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Select the session and freshness. Set the session, as-of line, and source before comparing one symbol with another.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Set the intake rules. Write the fields a symbol must carry: identity, coverage, freshness, and the required flow lens.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Keep stale rows out of the rank. A missing or stale field is a visible exclusion—not a value to average into attention.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Compare like with like. Use one universe, one session, one denominator, and one freshness line before reading relative attention.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Treat rank as a candidate list. Rank narrows where to inspect next; it does not assert direction, intent, or a trade decision.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Log the universe boundary. Save the symbol set, filters, timestamp, owner, and exclusions so another analyst can rerun the same view.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:08:00.000
Rank symbols without a signal. Next: S4E03 · inspect relative attention without turning the rank into a directional claim.
